# Gemini Prompt Engineering — Complete Reference

All AI logic lives in `src/lib/gemini.ts`. This file contains the following exported functions:

1. **VTON Pipeline (per pose)**: `generateVTONPrompt()` → `generateVTONImage()`
2. **VTON batch pre-pass (NEW)**: `analyzeBackgroundScene()` — runs ONCE per Generate batch when an inspiration background is provided; produces a deterministic frozen scene description that downstream `generateVTONPrompt` calls reuse VERBATIM.
3. **Model Swap Pipeline**: `generateModelSwapPrompt()` → `generateModelSwapImage()`

All Gemini calls accept an optional `abortSignal: AbortSignal` so a single user-initiated Stop can cancel every in-flight request in a generation batch (note: `AbortSignal` is client-only — the server may still complete and bill, see Cancellable Generation section).

## Two-Model Pipeline Architecture

| Step | Model ID | Model Name | Purpose | Config |
|------|----------|------------|---------|--------|
| Prompt Generation | `gemini-3-pro-preview` | Gemini 3 Pro | Analyzes reference images + parameters → detailed text prompt | `ThinkingLevel.LOW` |
| Image Generation | `gemini-3-pro-image-preview` | Nano Banana Pro | Takes prompt + reference images → generated image | `responseModalities: ["TEXT", "IMAGE"]`, `imageConfig: { aspectRatio, imageSize }` |

