### Enforcement Instructions (appended after prompt)
```
═══ CRITICAL: COMPLETE MODEL REPLACEMENT INSTRUCTIONS (NOT A FACE SWAP) ═══

1. First reference image is ORIGINAL product photo — preserve clothing EXACTLY
   (same garment, fit, colors, patterns, textures, construction, wrinkles, drape)

2. REPLACE ENTIRE HUMAN MODEL — not just face. Every visible body part
   (face, neck, shoulders, arms, hands, fingers, torso, legs, feet) must belong
   to the NEW person. Use their EXACT face, skin tone, hair color, hair style,
   body build, and proportions for the COMPLETE body.

3. ★★★ SKIN TONE UNIFORMITY (MOST CRITICAL) ★★★
   New model's skin tone PERFECTLY CONSISTENT across ALL visible body parts:
   - Face and neck: new model's skin tone
   - Arms and hands: SAME skin tone as face (not original model's)
   - Legs and feet (if visible): SAME skin tone as face
   - Décolletage/chest (if visible): SAME skin tone as face
   ZERO visible skin tone difference between face and any other body part.
   If new model has different skin tone than original, ENTIRE body reflects new tone uniformly.

4. New model must adopt EXACT SAME POSE as original — same body position,
   arm placement, leg stance, head angle.

5. {keepBackground: "Keep background IDENTICAL" : "Replace background as described"}

6. Clothing-to-body interaction natural on new model's proportions.

7. Maintain same camera angle, framing, professional photography quality.

