## Critical Rules for Prompt Modifications

### Clothing-Specific
- **Fit Override**: User's explicit fit selection is AUTHORITATIVE. If user selects "regular", the prompt MUST say "regular fit" even if the garment image looks oversized. Only if fit is null does the AI determine fit from images.
- **Product-Description Approach**: The clothing prompt asks Gemini Pro to analyze and describe every garment detail in text. This works because clothing detail preservation is best achieved through explicit textual description.
- **8 Critical Accuracy Requirements**: Never remove or weaken these — they're the backbone of clothing fidelity.
- **Garment Type Emphasis**: The hero garment (topwear/bottomwear/onepiece) gets maximum description detail; complementary items are secondary.

### Footwear-Specific
- **Scene-Focused, Images-First**: The footwear prompt DELIBERATELY does not describe product details. Gemini Pro must NOT describe specific colors, patterns, logos, or construction — doing so causes the image generator to follow text over photos, losing fidelity.
- **Brand-Blind**: NEVER name the brand in any prompt. The image generator will hallucinate incorrect logo variants from its world knowledge if it recognizes a brand name. All branding described as abstract visual shapes.
- **Images-First Architecture**: In `generateVTONImage()`, footwear reference images come FIRST in the content array, followed by other images, with text LAST. Less text = model pays more attention to images.
- **Product-Only Shots**: Model image is NOT passed. Prompt says "no human model". `requiresModel: false` on the pose.

### Model Swap-Specific
- **Full-Body Replacement**: The #1 failure mode is face-only swap with skin tone mismatch. Every instruction hammers "ENTIRE person, not just face".
- **Skin Tone Uniformity**: Repeated 4+ times in the prompt — face, neck, arms, hands, legs, feet must ALL match the new model's skin tone.
- **Clothing Preservation**: The clothing must remain pixel-perfect identical — zero changes to any garment attribute.
- **Pose Preservation**: The new model must adopt the exact same pose.
- **Background Handling**: `keep-same` preserves everything; `new-background` supports inspiration image, text, or default studio.

### Cross-Cutting Rules
- **Gender Context**: Always passed and used to inform garment analysis (male=broader shoulders/straighter cuts; female=varied necklines/darting; unisex=relaxed proportions).
- **View Angle**: Prompt describes ONLY details visible from the specified camera angle.
- **Framing**: Crop boundary is strict. "product-only" = NO human body. "waist-up" = NO lower body.
- **Model Reference**: When provided, prompt instructs "EXACT same person" reproduction. Skipped for product-only shots.
- **Accessories**: Two types — AI-chosen (no image, AI picks best match) and exact reference (with uploaded image, must match precisely).
- **Background**: Three modes — inspiration image, text description, or default studio.
- **All Prompts Live in gemini.ts**: Never scatter AI prompts across components.
